Model:
- Frames on a stack. Each frame: `{ indent, keys }` where `indent` is the indent of the mapping CONTENT it represents... let me define: a mapping frame pushed when we encounter a key K at indent I (non-list): this frame holds K's children → its content indent > I. I'll set frame.indent = I for key K (children have indent > I). Recording key K happens in the PARENT frame (top of stack after popping).

Processing a key line at indent I:
1. If inside block scalar: handled above (dedent ends it).
2. Determine effective indent for popping:
   - non-list key: pop while top.indent >= I. (A sibling at same indent pops the previous sibling's frame — correct. A child at deeper indent pops nothing since deeper frames have bigger indent... wait we pop top.indent >= I: if top is a child frame at indent J > I, J >= I → popped. Correct: moving from a child back to a shallower key pops all deeper frames.)
